2. PERMISSIONS GRANTED

   You may, free of charge and without asking permission:

   a) read, study and analyse the Software, for any purpose, including
      security research and academic work;

   b) compile, run and modify the Software on your own machines;

   c) quote excerpts of the Software in a security report, an article, a piece
      of research or a court document, provided the source is identified;

   d) publish the result of any analysis or audit of the Software, including a
      critical one, without prior notice to us and without our approval;

   e) deposit a verbatim copy of the Software in a public software archive
      (Software Heritage, the Internet Archive, or an equivalent), so that any
      analysis citing it stays verifiable if this repository moves or
      disappears;

   f) distribute a modified copy of the Software as a proof of concept, when it
      accompanies a published security report and serves to make that report
      reproducible. The copy must state that it is modified and must not be
      presented as a release.

3. RESTRICTIONS

   You may not, without prior written permission from EndlessLock:

   a) redistribute the Software, modified or not, in source or in binary form,
